bonfyre monitor — what your sources said about a business

Usage:
  bonfyre monitor --watch NAME [--watch OTHER-NAME] [--about TEXT] [options]

Finds every item in the item archive from the last --days that names the
business, then the local model reads each one: is it this business or a
namesake, what kind of mention, how it reflects, and whether to read it today.

Options:
  --watch NAME        A name to look for; repeat for other names it goes by
  --about TEXT        One line that tells this business apart from namesakes
  --days N            How far back to look (default 30)
  --limit N           Most items to read (default 40)
  --out FILE          Write the digest (.md) or the full report with receipts (.json)
  --json              Print the full report instead of the digest
  --archive FILE      Item archive (default $BONFYRE_ITEM_ARCHIVE_DB or ~/.bonfyre/estate-local/items.db)
  --model NAME        Prefer this local model (a file name or part of one);
                      otherwise the front loads the largest that fits
  --model-endpoint U  Local model server (default http://127.0.0.1:7000)

Example:
  bonfyre monitor --watch Target --about "Target Corporation, the US retail chain" --days 30 --out target.md
